<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Contract

Two surfaces compose the `~` sigil layer, and each answers a question the other cannot.

''The wikirule stays TS.'' `lar-sigil` registers as a TW5 wikirule (`module-type: wikirule`) over both the block and the inline phase. It claims block forms (container ahu, container pranala, generic-with-closer) at block parse and leaf inline forms (aka, kahea, loulou, inline pranala, ahu/kau invocation) at inline parse — work that runs inside TW5's parser and reaches no wikitext seam.

''The dispatcher stays wikitext.'' `\widget ~(name p1:"" … p5:"" args:"" src:"")` in `tiddlers/sigil-dispatcher.tid` transcludes the variable `~<name>`, so `<<~ WORD ARGS>>` reaches whatever definition this wiki holds under that name.

Dispatch model:
* every compound and simple sigil routes to the `~` dispatcher as `name=SIGIL, p1..p5=ARGS`
* block and inline pranala route to `~pranala` directly, on keyword args
* a generic block-with-closer passes through as a text literal

Child-slot detection (ahu, kau, and whatever the grammar adds next) reads `grammarChildSlotNames()`; the rule hardcodes no sigil name beyond what the grammar registry supplies.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-gradient-floor>>

!! The Gradient's Floor

A sigil a reader typed never disappears. TiddlyWiki renders a transclude's CHILDREN where the target resolves to nothing, so the dispatcher hands its own verbatim text — `src` — down as the transclude body, and a wiki that has never seen the procedure puts the sigil's text on the page. The floor rides as the parser's own fallback, never a second mechanism bolted beside it.

''The verbatim rides through `<$text>`, never through a variable reference.'' The text IS sigil syntax, so rendering it as wikitext would re-enter the rule that produced it. Literal text ends the recursion.

''An empty name names nothing.'' Definitions compose by handing the dispatcher a name they were given. An empty slot would make `addprefix` yield the bare `~` — the dispatcher's OWN name — and the transclude would re-enter itself until the stack ended. `!is[blank]` empties the variable instead, and an empty variable resolves to nothing, landing on the floor already standing.

A sigil form the rule cannot recognize renders as `<span class="lar-sigil-degraded lar-sigil-<grade>">` carrying its verbatim text, and the rule files a diagnostic at the matched span so the filter and the gate see the same damage the render plane shows.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/slots-and-runs>>

!! A Slot and a Run Answer Different Questions

`p1 … p5` hold positional slots — one value each, delimiters stripped, `name=value` pairs stepped over. `args` carries the argument run exactly as written, for the definitions that read a SHAPE rather than an arity: an edge annotation whose from, arrow and to compose one assertion, and `kau`, which runs its own parse over `#fragment name props`.

''Neither derives from the other,'' so neither can be got subtly wrong in the definitions that read them.

<<~/ahu>>

